ly chain services, including design and development, new product introduction, engineering services, component sourcing, electronics manufacturing and assembly, testing, mechanical assembly, systems integration, precision machining, logistics, asset management, product licensing, and after-market repair and return services. It also provides hardware platform solutions, which includes development of infrastructure platforms, and hardware and software design solutions and services, including open-source software that can be used as-is or customized for specific applications; and management of program, including design and supply chain, manufacturing, and after-market support, including IT asset disposition and asset management services. The company offers its products and services to original equipment manufacturers, and cloud-based and other service providers, including hyperscalers, and other companies in aerospace and defense, industrial, HealthTech, capital equipment, communications, and enterprise markets. The company has a strategic collaboration with Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. for the development of Helios, a rack-scale AI platform. The company was incorporated in 1994 and is headquartered in Toronto, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert Andrew Mionis | CEO & Chair of the Board | Age 62 | Compensation: $5.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 23K people. Revenue per employee of $521K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $19K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Celestica, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $26.1B market cap on $12.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 31% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 19-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 11% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $458M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.79\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 20\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $88.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 9% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Celestica (TSX:CLS) Rides the AI Wave: What Is Behind the Raised Targets?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/ca/stocks/technology/celestica-tsxcls-rides-the-ai-wave-what-is-behind-the-raised-targets","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793991840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Does Buyback Timing Matter for Celestica (TSX:CLS) Tech Investors?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/ca/stocks/technology/does-buyback-timing-matter-for-celestica-tsxcls-tech-investors","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793922900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Is Cash Resilience Fuelling Celestica (TSX:CLS) Growth Story Further?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/ca/stocks/growth/is-cash-re